# Keep the build context small and make sure host build artifacts never leak
# into the image. The image builds everything itself from the pinned sources.
# Only what the Dockerfile COPYs must survive these exclusions:
# package.json/package-lock.json, client/, relay/, server/, cypress/,
# cypress.config.ts and docker/run-tests.sh.

# Host build artifacts and dependencies
**/node_modules
**/.lake
client/dist
relay/dist
games
logs
cypress/screenshots
cypress/videos

# Version-control and editor/CI metadata
.git
.github
.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# Docs - not needed inside the image
doc
*.md
LICENSE
NOTES*

# Note: docker/docker-compose.yml is passed to the CLI explicitly and
# docker/run-tests.sh is baked into the image, so the docker/ folder stays in
# the context. The Dockerfile is read directly by the builder, not copied.